# Doru, the priest's son, in the undercroft (docs/voice/doru.md)

~ start
if flag.doru_spoken_to and not flag.donavich_mercy_blessing
-> again
endif
set doru_spoken_to
if flag.donavich_mercy_blessing
-> blessed
endif
cutscene doru_ceiling
Narrator: Something crosses the ceiling, quick and flat as a spider, and settles above you. A young man's face hangs upside down in the dark, smiling.
Doru [sly]: Father? No. You smell like outside. Like rain and roads. I'd forgotten roads. Come closer; I can't see you properly.
interject class:cleric: Stay back from him. He's starving, and he's looking at our throats.
-> menu

# Coming back down after the first meeting: he's where you left him, and the picture and the first words don't repeat.
~ again
Narrator: Doru still clings to the ceiling above the cells, exactly where you left him. Only his eyes have moved.
Doru [sly]: You came back. Nobody comes back. Did you bring Father, or just your throats?
-> menu

~ menu
* Who are you? -> who
* What happened to you at the castle? -> castle
* [Insight DC 13] What does he really want? -> insight_ok | insight_fail
* [Cleric] Pray for him. -> pray
* We'll let you out. -> free_warn
* This ends now. Attack him. -> fight
* We'll leave you here. -> leave

~ who
Doru: Doru. The priest's son. I rang the bell on holy days, before. I was going to be a hero. Everyone was going to sing about it.
-> menu

~ castle
Doru [sad]: We went up the road with torches, singing. The gates were open. He met us in the hall in a beautiful coat and said we must be hungry after such a climb.
Doru [afraid]: He fed us. He let us talk about killing him all through the meal, smiling. Then the candles went out. I was dessert, he said. The others weren't so lucky. Or they were.
-> menu

~ insight_ok
Narrator: He's counting your throats. Every plea comes with a glance at the stair behind you, measuring the distance.
-> menu

~ insight_fail
Narrator: He looks like a frightened young man, and nothing in his face says otherwise.
-> menu

~ pray
Doru [angry]: Stop. Stop it, it burns. No, keep going. Father used to... stop! Stop!
Narrator: For a heartbeat the hunger leaves his face, and a scared boy looks down at you. Then it comes back.
inspire class:cleric: prayed for a vampire spawn who used to be a boy
-> menu

~ free_warn
Doru [smile]: You would? Oh, you would. I'll go far away. To the castle; the master will take me in. I'll never trouble Father again. I swear it on the Morninglord. On my mother. On anything.
interject tag:blunt: He's a hungry wolf asking us to open the pen.
* Go, then. The way is open. -> free
* On second thought, no. -> menu

~ free
set doru_freed
quest the_priests_son doru_freed
Narrator: He's past you before the words are finished, a rush of cold air up the stair. Somewhere above, a door bangs, and the bell rope thrums once, as if something brushed it going over the wall.
approve kip_smudgewick -3 liriel_dawnsong -2 godrick_pendlebrook -2 ratatoille -2 thistle -1: You let a starving vampire spawn loose on the village
-> END

~ fight
Doru [angry]: Then come up here and do it.
combat doru_undercroft

~ leave
set doru_left_locked
quest the_priests_son doru_left
Doru [angry]: Go, then! Go! I'll be here. I'm always here. Tell Father I'm hungry. Tell him every night!
Narrator: You back up the stair. The voice follows you, pleading, then cursing, then pleading again.
-> END

~ blessed
Narrator: The young face on the ceiling looks at the holy water in your hands, then at the open door above, and understands.
Doru [sad]: He sent you. Didn't he. He finally said yes. Tell him I'm sorry about the cake on his name day. Tell him... quickly. Before I stop being sorry.
* Rest now, Doru. -> blessed_fight
* [Cleric] We'll pray for you while we do it. -> blessed_prayer

~ blessed_prayer
Narrator: The prayer begins. Doru closes his eyes, and for one breath his lips move with it.
inspire class:cleric: prayed Doru out of the world
approve liriel_dawnsong +2: You prayed for Doru as he went
-> blessed_fight

~ blessed_fight
Narrator: The boy is gone between one breath and the next. What drops from the ceiling is only hunger.
combat doru_undercroft
